d but I think Sam darn old when  you look at the safest pick and I don't  always think the safest pick is the  right pick but if if I were Cleveland I  think Sam Donald is the guy based on  their history that they should go after  so I mean how is it possible and I and I  and I fully admittedly ask you this  question Troy as somebody who's been  talking about this draft pretty much  every day for months and and and by  months I also mean last year when we  were talking at the draft last year in  Philadelphia that this year would be the  year  in which there would be tons of  franchise quarterbacks available how is  it possible that we're now here and that  there would be some talent evaluators  including yourself that think that there  might not be any franchise quarterbacks  in this year well I hate rich every year  every year there is a best quarterback  in the draft and and so every year but  that doesn't mean that there's a  franchise quarterback but that's easy  for me as I sit here in my chair in my  office and say that but if you're a  general manager and you don't have a  quarterback it's hard to pass up on a  guy who who is the best or who you think  is the best in this case there's there's  more than just one particular guy but  we've seen we've seen over the years I  don't want to name names but we've seen  guys who have gone early in the draft or  at least have been first-round picks and  once they get into the NFL you're left  kind of scratching your head you're  saying really what was what was it that  they liked and and again III wish all  these guys the best of luck I hope they  all go on and have Hall of Fame careers  I you know I I know how hard the  position is but the history would say  that that's not going to be the case and  I don't want to say that people last  year overvalued these guys I think Sam  Donald for instance was a guy who could  come off a really great freshman year  redshirt freshman year and then you know  wasn't quite as good t