e on Baker Mayfield and I like a lot  you know I will say that watching him in  college I got real worn out just every  time the camera was on him that he was  talking or yelling at some opponent or  whatever it was and and then I really  studied him on tape and and I think the  guy can really play he's the most  productive of the group he's accurate  with the football he's got plenty of arm  strength and and I believe that he is I  think he has the skills that translate  to the NFL the height I know is a  concern and I know you can't point to  many people many quarterbacks under six  one that have had success but I have  always felt I felt this when Doug Flutie  was coming out in the NFL Draft I  thought height at the time was overrated  I've continued to think that and even at  six four there were times I couldn't see  receivers because of the offensive  lineman that were in front of me and  it's about throwing through windows and  he's been able to do that he's been  highly successful doing it III really I  think he and Rose are the two guys of  the guys I've seen are the only two that  I think can step into a pro team a play  on week one troy aikman here on the Rich  Eisen show what about Josh Allen the  questions of his accuracy knowing as you  do about the transition from one level  to the other and obviously losing two  before you can win Troy what what can  you tell me about Josh Allen's accuracy  issues that  give you pause well I you know when we  first preface the answer by saying with  Sam darn old he's had problems  protecting the football and I believe  that with tough coaching and good  coaching you can coach a lot of that out  of a quarterback I believe when it comes  to accuracy yeah I know they've worked  on tightening up his throwing motion and  his stride and some of the things as  mechanics and some of the things that  that maybe lead to some inaccuracies but  in my experience in watching  quarterbacks you you can either put the  ball where you 