resigning him I think it just says that  this goes way beyond you know what he  has done or what he's capable of doing  on the football field  what do you mean by Garrett guys though  I mean that that was the one thing that  I that gave me pause when I heard what  he said to Jane Slater on the NFL  Network that Garrett guys well I will  say there's always I don't know to  answer that I know Jason Garrett is a  friend of mine I have not spoken to him  since since Dez was released I'm not  exactly sure you know what that means  although I do know that having been in  locker rooms there are players that are  perceived you know like there's teachers  pets or whatever there are players who  are perceived as hey you know they'll  beat the drum for this coach or this  coat you know they're all in on this  particular coach I to be honest with you  in my conversations with Dez Bryant and  certainly my conversations with Jason  Garrett over the years I would have I  would have guessed that Dez Bryant was  it was a Garrett guy so you know when he  made those comments I was a little  surprised by that I think a lot of  people were I know Jason Witten was  offended by that I think that locker  room is I think it's been a very  close-knit group and they were all very  protective of Dez over the years and I  think they were all a little stunned and  and I don't say they're hurt they're big  boys but I don't think they like the way  that he walked out and and maybe through  some of them under the bus  Troy really appreciate the time as  always great seeing you yesterday really  look forward to working with you chat  with a bond be great all right Troy  thanks to the call you got that straight  the Rich Eisen show weekdays at noon  eastern on audience

